PILOT PERMISSION

Permission is granted to a church taking part in a Preekstof pilot, and to Donkey Mobile
B.V. and its employees for the purpose of evaluating the software and supporting those
churches, to:

  - download, install and run this software on their own computers;
  - use the clips it produces without restriction, including publicly and commercially,
    for the church's own communication;
  - change configuration, templates, brand presets and word lists for their own use.

Under these conditions:

  - the software is not passed on to anyone outside the pilot, published, resold, or
    offered as a service to third parties;
  - this notice stays with any copy;
  - the permission may be withdrawn in writing, after which the software is no longer run,
    while clips already produced remain the church's own.

Anything beyond this needs a separate written agreement. Ask; the answer is usually yes.


THE PARTS THAT ARE NOT MINE

This software is built on other people's work, some of it shipped alongside and some of it
fetched on first use. That work carries its own terms, which this licence does not change
and cannot override. NOTICE lists every piece, where it comes from and under what licence.
Read it before distributing anything.


